# Partita No. 5 in G major, BWV 829: Gigue (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: the last movement, a three-voice fugal gigue in 6/8. The
# subject is a dotted, leaping figure (an upbeat, then a dotted eighth
# and a falling broken chord ending in a leap of an octave or fifth);
# the second half brings a new subject with a trill in it and then
# combines it with the first. Brilliant and bouncing, with a steady
# two-in-a-bar.
#
# Time signature: 6/8 with an eighth-note upbeat; 64 bars. Two halves,
# each repeated in the score: A from the upbeat to bar 32 (which ends
# with B's upbeat), B bars 33-64 (Mutopia 57title-hub.mid / 57hub.ly,
# "7. Gigue"). The MIDI plays each half once.
#
# Repeats: with both repeats the song is 12418 bytes, over the
# jukebox's 9472-byte limit. Played once through it is 6238; with only
# the first half repeated it is 9218 and fits. So only A is repeated:
# A A B. Taking the first repeat alone is a choice harpsichordists
# sometimes make in a long gigue; it keeps the exposition heard twice
# (once as an echo) and the fugal second half once, where its new
# subject and the combination are fresh.
#
# Bars as performed (play, from the upbeat at 0.8333):
#   A first time 0.83-32.83   A repeat 32.83-64.83   B 64.83-96
#   Score bar x of A is x+32 in the repeat; score bar x of B (33-64)
#   is x+32.
#
# Tempo: dotted quarter = 56 (eighth = 168), as performed about 3:26.
# Confirmed track time: Angela Hewitt (2018 recording, AHCD030, her own
# listing) 4:24 for the movement, which with both repeats (128 bars) is
# about dotted quarter = 58; without them it would be an implausible
# 29. I could not confirm other timings for this movement (Schiff's and
# Gould's track lists did not show it). 56 is a shade under Hewitt: the
# sixteenths are 5 frames each and the trills in B faster still, so a
# quicker tempo would blur them on the chip.
#
# Structure (my reading of the score):
#   A  0-2    subject in the middle voice, G major, from the upbeat.
#      2-4    answer in the top voice on D.
#      6-8    subject in the bass, G major.
#      9-12   episode, the bass in broken sixteenths.
#      13-14  subject in the bass on D.
#      15-18  chain of suspensions in the upper voices over the bass's
#             sixteenths.
#      19-20  subject in the middle voice on D.
#      23-25  the subject's head in sequence, top and bass together.
#      26-32  to D major: the subject in the top (30-31), cadence on D.
#   B  33-45  a new subject with a trill (bass 33, top 35, middle 41),
#             through E minor.
#      46-50  the first subject returns: bass in E minor (46), top in
#             A minor (50), against the trilled one.
#      51-54  the trilled subject again.
#      55-60  the first subject in the bass in G (55), then the middle
#             (60): home key.
#      61-64  trills in the bass in rising steps, final cadence in G.
#
# Plan: A full the first time and echoed for its repeat; B full, with
# the last step up where the first subject returns in G (score 55).
# The subject is brought forward where it enters in the bass or top.
# Bass notes below B2 are lifted an octave by the converter, which
# blunts the bass in the closing octaves a little.

pickup 8
tempo 56 4.
play 0.8333-32.8333 0.8333-32.8333 32.8333-64

voice mid 1           # the middle voice a step back, except where led

dyn 1 mf              # A, first time
lead 3-4 top          # answer, top, on D
lead 7-8 bottom       # subject, bass, G
lead 13-14 bottom     # subject, bass, on D
lead 19-20 mid        # subject, middle voice, on D
lead 30-31 top        # subject, top, D major

dyn 32.8333 mp        # A repeat, from its upbeat: echo
lead 35-36 top        # the same entries in the repeat (score + 32)
lead 39-40 bottom
lead 45-46 bottom
lead 51-52 mid
lead 62-63 top
broaden 63-64 0.95    # the D major cadence at the end of A, before B

dyn 64.8333 mf        # B, from its upbeat
lead 65-66 bottom     # score 33: the trilled subject, bass
lead 78-79 bottom     # score 46: first subject returns, bass, E minor
lead 82-83 top        # score 50: first subject, top, A minor
dyn 87 f              # score 55-64: the first subject home in G, to
lead 87-88 bottom     # the end; bass entry

rit 2 0.75            # performed 95-96 (score 63-64): final cadence
